Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:04:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NetworkPolicy: give restored apps their network access back
 once

Before "don't cut off apps that request INTERNET at PACKAGE_ADDED", the package
receiver gave POLICY_REJECT_ALL to apps Play restored as archived installs (no
APK, so no permissions), and the block outlived the real APK. That change stops
new blocks; this one heals the existing ones, once, through a new Lineage
policy-file version (3).

Only apps installed for a device restore or setup that request and hold
INTERNET are cleared, so blocks users set on other apps stay. Install reasons
are kept only for users who already had the package installed, so an unarchive
can replace the restore reason; every app left blocked is logged with its
install reason ("Keeping REJECT_ALL for uid=...") to show whether this needs to
reach further. requestsInternetPermission() moves out of the package receiver
so both paths share it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
